From a21787b3a3d4e1bfc797479044bd92263fcca456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Danylo Piliaiev <dpiliaiev@igalia.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:22:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tu: Properly wait for mem writes to finish in
 emit_copy_query_pool_results

emit_copy_query_pool_results may read from `available_iova` twice:
- First time via CP_COND_EXEC that doesn't WAIT_FOR_ME;
- Second time via CP_MEM_TO_MEM which does implicit WAIT_FOR_ME.

Thus they can disagree on availability, so that from VK user perspective
`availability == 1` but value is garbage.

Fixes flaky:
```
dEQP-VK.transform_feedback.simple*query_with_availability*
```

Cc: mesa-stable
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Danylo Piliaiev <dpiliaiev@igalia.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46628>
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc
index 70e6c9dfcea..7cd5688b72e 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc
@@ -858,9 +858,6 @@ emit_copy_query_pool_results(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
                              VkDeviceSize stride,
                              VkQueryResultFlags flags)
 {
-   /* Flush cache for the buffer to copy to. */
-   tu_emit_cache_flush<CHIP>(cmdbuf);
-
    /* From the Vulkan 1.1.130 spec:
     *
     *    vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults is guaranteed to see the effect of previous
@@ -870,7 +867,12 @@ emit_copy_query_pool_results(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
     * To ensure that previous writes to the available bit are coherent, first
     * wait for all writes to complete.
     */
-   tu_cs_emit_pkt7(cs, CP_WAIT_MEM_WRITES, 0);
+   cmdbuf->state.cache.flush_bits |= TU_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_MEM_WRITES |
+                                     /* For CP_COND_EXEC */
+                                     TU_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_FOR_ME;
+
+   /* Flush cache for the buffer to copy to. */
+   tu_emit_cache_flush<CHIP>(cmdbuf);
 
    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < queryCount; i++) {
       uint32_t query = firstQuery + i;
-- 
